## 9. Decisions this asks for

| # | Decision | Owner | Recommendation |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Collapse seven stages to five with Parked as a state | Mark | Yes; the Opportunity and Discovery split has no definition and no calibration |
| 2 | System-sent email after approval, on the rep's behalf, in legal markets and warm threads | Oliver, Phil for compliance comfort | Yes, batch-approved each morning; LinkedIn stays manual |
| 3 | Plays as the single automation concept, replacing the hardcoded chase sequence | Brad, Oliver | Yes; build the runner once, express the current sequence as the first play |
| 4 | Retire the Activities board concept; tasks only for non-message actions | Oliver | Yes; a sent message is an interaction |
| 5 | Drop Health and Stage status as labels; keep them as sort and filter | Oliver, Jack | Yes; the labels were a monday workaround |
| 6 | Weekly report first, dashboard second | Mark | Yes; the report is what was asked for |
