THE MANUAL WORKAROUND LOSES THE RECORD, and this is the part that will hurt later. A message copied out and sent by hand is a touch Lovable did not write. The four hourly watcher picks up LinkedIn DMs, so those should reconcile. InMails are the risk: LinkedIn's own export has never contained InMails, so if the watcher does not capture them directly there is no route back and they are gone. See i048.
PRACTICAL SUGGESTION WHILE THIS IS BROKEN: send DMs by hand, because they are recoverable, and hold InMails until send works. If an InMail genuinely cannot wait, write down who and when at the moment of sending, not afterwards.

A REVISION MAY STILL BE WRITTEN ON FAILURE. One draft showed PREVIOUS DRAFTS 3 on a contact where nothing has been sent. Worth checking whether failed AI edits or regenerations leave partial revisions behind, because a silent bad revision is worse than the visible error.

TWO THINGS STILL WORKING WELL, worth saying since this report is all bad news. The guardrails generate correctly and specifically, for instance do not name Helvetia, AIG or Helvetic Warranty by name, do not cite the volume estimate or any commission figures, do not reference Stolle, Teuteberg or any warm intro path. And the AI state of play panel is writing a proper record of what each draft did and why. Both are the hard parts, and neither is affected.

THE SAME SCREENS KEEP SHOWING i067: Beste Gruesse, Oli, now on a fourth draft. And i084 stands, LINT 100 while a displayed guardrail is broken.$il$);
